045417] [17592186087853 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087853 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding a Horizontal Asymptote When the Degree of the Numerator is Greater" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087853 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186087580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087853 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "653503b2-4631-561e-af5e-847bcbdfe8e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087896 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186088778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087896 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186088779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087896 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186088780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087896 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186088781 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087896 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087896 #edb/ref 1045 "Horizontal Asymptotes of Rational Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087896 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186088778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087896 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186087896 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "10d02fcd-c546-5af1-b0ee-b92aa67beb52" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088778 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186088779 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088778 #edb/ref 1061 467901 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088778 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1492a6f8-d490-54b0-9792-5135334cf77f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088778 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186088939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088779 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186088780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088779 #edb/ref 1061 467902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088779 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6e2fe124-312a-5cc5-b3f0-cf7d27eed5e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088779 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186087851 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088780 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186088781 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088780 #edb/ref 1061 467905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088780 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6d02fb4e-b4fe-507b-989d-d5d424b86da7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088780 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186087852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088781 #edb/ref 1061 467909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088781 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ddb86f2d-2c95-5000-bebe-6a05a5fa5338" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088781 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186087853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088939 #edb/ref 1064 "A **horizontal asymptote** is a horizontal line that a graph of a function approaches as $x$ tends to (positive or negative) infinity.\n\nFor example, let's consider the rational function\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\frac{2x^2}{x^2-1}.\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/ec/ec8071dc9280cf344126ec3d6d9287823fc81c3ade910c98191a1d4d43ec0d6e.png)\n\nWe can see that $y=f(x)$ has the horizontal asymptote $y=2.$ The function gets closer and closer to this line but never touches it.\n\nBut how can we calculate the horizontal asymptote of a function without using a graph?\n\nTo find the horizontal asymptote of a rational function, we follow these three steps.\n\n- Identify the **dominant term** in the denominator. The dominant term is the leading term of the polynomial in the denominator, though we usually ignore the coefficient.\n\n- Divide every term in the numerator and denominator of $f(x)$ by the dominant term.\n\n- Evaluate the remaining expression as $x\\to\\infty.$\n\nIn our case, the dominant term is $x^2.$ So, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by $x^2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}}{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen $x$ is very large, the $\\dfrac{1}{x^2}$term becomes very small. Therefore, as $x\\to\\infty,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(\\frac{2}{1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & \\to \\frac{2}{1-0} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088939 #edb/ref 1065 3776 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088939 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "d23ef418-713b-5f13-8463-2cd30f9458e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088939 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378422 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186378423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378422 #edb/ref 1069 "q-113180" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378422 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378422 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the horizontal asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3x+2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378422 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4507ae6a-461d-5502-b3e2-7bf57bad8732" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378422 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the horizontal asymptote of a rational function, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by the dominant term in the denominator, and then we let $x\\to \\infty .$\n\nIgnoring the coefficient, the dominant term in the denominator is $x.$ So, we divide every term in the numerator and denominator by $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3x+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{x})}{(\\frac{3x}{x}+\\frac{2}{x})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(3+\\frac{2}{x})}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when $x$ is very large, the term $\\frac{2}{x}$ becomes very small. Therefore, as $x\\to \\infty ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{(3+\\frac{2}{x})} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3+0} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is not a constant, which means that $y=f(x)$ does not have a horizontal asymptote." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378423 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378423 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378423 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378423 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378423 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378423 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378423 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378423 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186378425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378423 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "219e25d5-1a5d-54bd-84e6-7016995fdf31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378424 #edb/ref 1080 "y=3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378424 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378424 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8f3bea2c-306c-5e48-88e0-f498569d09ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378425 #edb/ref 1080 "No horizontal asymptotes" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378425 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378425 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "10399da4-e690-5c4d-b2a4-9bff2c1171d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378426 #edb/ref 1080 "y=\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378426 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378426 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a1078051-d4e1-5037-957d-9cb4bee113ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378427 #edb/ref 1080 "y=2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378427 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378427 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0308c1f2-6766-5c2d-93c2-954e116c5e2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378428 #edb/ref 1080 "y=\\frac{1}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378428 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378428 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c831d6cb-31f4-5404-8eed-6b17d2e24673" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423002 #edb/ref 1080 "y=-1,\\,2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423002 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423002 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4ec2ab89-ebdf-50c8-bf29-dc40d7200760" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423012 #edb/ref 1080 "No horizontal asymptotes" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423012 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921